{"text":"its zero is the zero: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:_:)"},{"text":" makes it one, and so does a product in which either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component reaches its zero, so no path is half reached.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The laws hold when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"First"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s ⊗ keeps strict order on both sides: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a < b"},{"type":"text","text":" gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊗ c < b ⊗ c"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"c ⊗ a < c ⊗ b"},{"type":"text","text":" for every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"c"},{"type":"text","text":" other than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":". Integer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TropicalSemiring"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MaxPlusSemiring"},{"type":"text","text":" values keep it (floating point up to rounding), so the lexicographic product"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of either with any selective semiring is a selective semiring, and Dijkstra’s algorithm,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Bellman–Ford and the other selective entry points give best pairs. A bottleneck or Boolean"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first"},{"type":"text","text":" does not keep it: a narrow edge can tie two paths of different widths, and ⊕ then no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"longer distributes."}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Shortest paths, the fewest edges among equals.","graph.dijkstraShortestPaths(from: s) { LexicographicSemiring(TropicalSemiring(length[$0]), TropicalSemiring(1)) }"]}]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Se